# Project Structure

```
app/           # main.cpp + isolated test entry points
src/
  component/   # one .h per component (+ .cpp only if non-trivial helpers)
  system/      # systems grouped by cohesion
  entity/      # one *Factory per entity type
  (root)       # contexts, config, assets, utilities
tests/         # Catch2 unit tests
res/           # runtime assets
```

## `component/` — one file per component

Header contains: (1) plain-data `struct`, (2) `bagel::Storage<>` specialization, (3) conversion/inspect helpers that only touch that component (e.g. `Transform.h`). Add new headers to `Components.h`.

## `system/` — grouped by cohesion

Share a file when systems share file-local `static` state or are always one logical unit. Split when a `.cpp` is hard to navigate or concerns diverge. Register in `Systems.h`.

## `entity/` — one `*Factory` per type

`*Factory` suffix avoids collisions with component headers (`Cup.h` vs `CupFactory.h`). Factory creates entity, calls `addAll(...)`, returns it. File-local helpers stay in the same `.cpp`, never in headers. Register in `Entities.h`.

## `src/` root

Contexts (`RenderContext`, `PhysicsContext`), config (`GameConfig.h`), asset wrappers (`Assets`, `AssetManager`, `Texture`), and small utilities — not components or systems.

## `app/` — entry points

For isolated feature tests: dedicated `my_test.cpp` + first line of `app/CMakeLists.txt` sets `APP_SOURCES`. Remove before merging to `main`.

## Where does new code go?

| Question | Location |
|----------|----------|
| Data-only struct entities carry? | `component/MyThing.h` → `Components.h` |
| Converts/reads only that component? | Same component header |
| Per-frame logic over entities? | `system/` → `Systems.h` |
| Constructs a specific entity? | `entity/MyThingFactory.{h,cpp}` → `Entities.h` |
| Shared infrastructure? | `src/` root |
